{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/838","id":5115855899,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTatV2s8AAAABMO3EGw","html_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/838","diff_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/838.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pull/838.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/issues/838","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/838/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/838/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/issues/838/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/statuses/7a38251a07c17914e6cad7e6901f0a7330507648","number":838,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Sounding Line: measure metadata-only noncampaign custody in shadow","user":{"login":"Kgray44","id":64373011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64373011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44","html_url":"https://github.com/Kgray44","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kgray44/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ordinary campaign custody currently hydrates the complete base/candidate blob snapshots even when the installed reserve command returns `campaign=false` before campaign work. This adds a separate manual metadata-only shadow experiment to measure that route against an authenticated full-checkout baseline. Production ordinary checkout remains FULL_SNAPSHOT.\n\nThe planner requires complete base/candidate inventories, unchanged pinned installed readers and metadata contracts, unchanged attributes, and bounded metadata paths. Held owner lanes, campaign matches, reader drift and uncertainty retain FULL fallback. Every result remains `applied:false` and grants no source certificate. The manual pilot checks the actual installed reserve command under network/non-Git process denial, preserves original command frames and source identities, and reports checkout/reserve/source batching costs separately. It cannot write a Mainline Decision or substitute preparation.\n\nValidation: 15 focused selection/pilot tests and the owning workflow-admission test passed with no failures or skips; targeted formatting and lint passed. An exact-head Windows development fixture exercised real metadata fetch, protected hydration and the actual reserve CLI: campaign=false, zero network/non-Git process attempts, unchanged selected filesystem, complete 4,697-commit/31,570-tree ancestry, 18 blobs totaling 10,610,239 bytes. Reserve took 7,255 ms; setup plus reserve took 72,104 ms. These local timings are not a native hosted comparison. Original evidence remains preserved and the disposable fixture retired.\n\nCandidate: 7a38251a07c17914e6cad7e6901f0a7330507648; base: 613b73b5622e91dbee7b13c69ac7c5904771390e. Native pilot dispatch requires separately reviewed landed source and its own successful ordinary qualification as baseline. Activation, production performance acceptance and preparation reuse remain gated on independent native equivalence/adversarial evidence.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-